  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Inside Lang Ya blessed land, after Fang Yuan suppresses Lang Ya land spirit and takes the Thieving Heaven true inheritance there, he unleashes the immortal killer move Steal Life with Steal Life Immortal Gu as the core. Lang Ya land spirit inside the formation fires the move for him with Long Hair’s immortal essence; a finger-thick red light hits Thunder Ghost True Monarch’s forehead, she ages to death in moments, and her lifespan is fully consumed. Fang Yuan notes that bare use of Steal Life Immortal Gu does not distinguish ally from enemy, while this killer move he deduced targets only the enemy. Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable’s method still limits the Immortal Gu to three uses; Fang Yuan cannot remove that limit and spends one use on her.",
      "chapters": [
        1759
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "inh_thieving_heaven_true_inheritance",
        "sys_killer_moves",
        "gu_steal_life_gu",
        "char_thunder_ghost_true_monarch",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Steal Life Immortal Gu steals lifespan-related dao marks and shortens a person’s life. Thieving Heaven’s will states that normal use steals others’ lifespan, that the killer move he created can raise the user’s own lifespan (inferior to lifespan Gu), and that reverse use gives the user’s lifespan to another target.",
      "chapters": [
        1782
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "thieving-heaven-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_heavens_will",
        "gu_lifespan_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "That own-lifespan killer move is not the enemy-targeting Steal Life Fang Yuan deduced at Lang Ya.",
      "chapters": [
        1759
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "thieving-heaven-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_lang_ya_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fighting Duke Long, Fang Yuan closes in and lands Steal Life; Duke Long freezes briefly and asks how the move is in his hands.",
      "chapters": [
        1836
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "against-duke-long",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing lasting happens to Duke Long. He explains that heavenly dragon’s last stand makes his lifespan dwindle as his strength rises, blocks ordinary lifespan extension methods, and that Steal Life only influences lifespan dao marks, which may be why it failed. Fang Yuan still treats the move as a threat to most other Heavenly Court immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        1837
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "against-duke-long",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
